{
  "$comment": "GENERATED from the real jscad-raspberrypi V1 camera factories, by calling CameraModuleV1/V2/V3(), HQCameraModule(flipTripodMount) and ArducamHQCameraModule() and reading parts[name].getBounds() inside a checkout of that repository (it is not an npm dependency here, which is why there is no scripts/generate-* companion - see raspberrypi.cameraModule.spec.js for the exact procedure). Do not hand-edit. All values are millimetres, Z-up, in V1's own frame: the board is centred on x and y at the origin with its underside on z = 0, which is what Parts.Cube(...).Center() leaves behind (Center() aligns on xy only, never z). Each entry is [[minX,minY,minZ],[maxX,maxY,maxZ]] of that part's bounding box. V1's aggregate subassembly entries - 'hole', 'mounts', 'pins', and the 'holeshole0'/'mountsmount0'/'pinspin0' prefixed subpart names - are kept verbatim; the spec maps them onto this port's flat hole0/mount0/pin0 names.",
